**Chrome Plugin: Page Saver**
================================

**Overview**
------------

This Chrome plugin allows users to save the contents of the current page with a single click. The saved content is stored in a text file and can be downloaded or viewed within the plugin.

**Structure**
-------------

*   `manifest.json`: The plugin's metadata and permissions.
*   `popup.html`: The HTML for the popup that appears when the user clicks the plugin's icon.
*   `popup.js`: The JavaScript code that handles the popup's functionality.
*   `content.js`: The JavaScript code that retrieves the page content.
*   `icon.png`: The plugin's icon.

**Code**
-----

### manifest.json

```json
{
  "manifest_version": 3,
  "name": "Page Saver",
  "version": "1.0",
  "description": "Save the contents of the current page",
  "permissions": ["activeTab"],
  "action": {
    "default_popup": "popup.html",
    "default_icon": "icon.png"
  },
  "content_scripts": [
    {
      "matches": ["<all_urls>"],
      "js": ["content.js"]
    }
  ]
}
```

### popup.html

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
  <head>
    <title>Page Saver</title>
    <style>
      body {
        width: 200px;
        height: 100px;
        font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
        text-align: center;
      }
    </style>
  </head>
  <body>
    <h1>Page Saver</h1>
    <button id="save-btn">Save Page</button>
    <button id="view-btn">View Saved Page</button>
    <pre id="page-content"></pre>
    <script src="popup.js"></script>
  </body>
</html>
```

### popup.js

```javascript
document.addEventListener("DOMContentLoaded", function () {
  const saveBtn = document.getElementById("save-btn");
  const viewBtn = document.getElementById("view-btn");
  const pageContent = document.getElementById("page-content");

  saveBtn.addEventListener("click", function () {
    chrome.tabs.query({ active: true, currentWindow: true }, function (tabs) {
      chrome.tabs.sendMessage(tabs[0].id, { action: "savePage" });
    });
  });

  viewBtn.addEventListener("click", function () {
    chrome.storage.local.get("pageContent", function (data) {
      if (data.pageContent) {
        pageContent.innerText = data.pageContent;
      }
    });
  });
});
```

### content.js

```javascript
function savePage() {
  const pageHTML = document.documentElement.outerHTML;
  chrome.storage.local.set({ pageContent: pageHTML });
  const blob = new Blob([pageHTML], { type: "text/html" });
  const url = URL.createObjectURL(blob);
  const a = document.createElement("a");
  a.href = url;
  a.download = "saved-page.html";
  a.click();
}

chrome.runtime.onMessage.addListener(function (request, sender, sendResponse) {
  if (request.action === "savePage") {
    savePage();
  }
});
```

**Usage**
-----

1.  Create a new folder for your plugin and create the files mentioned above.
2.  In the Chrome browser, navigate to `chrome://extensions/`.
3.  Enable "Developer mode" and click "Load unpacked".
4.  Select the folder containing your plugin's files.
5.  The plugin should now be visible in the browser toolbar.
6.  Click the plugin's icon to open the popup.
7.  Click the "Save Page" button to save the contents of the current page.
8.  Click the "View Saved Page" button to view the saved page content within the popup.

Note: This plugin saves the entire page content, including HTML, CSS, and JavaScript code. If you want to save only the visible content, you may need to modify the `savePage` function in `content.js` accordingly.

