**Nginx Helper Cache Purge Plugin**
====================================

This WordPress plugin clears all Nginx helper cache when a plugin or theme is added, updated, or changed.

**Installation**
---------------

1. Upload the `nginx-helper-cache-purge` folder to the `/wp-content/plugins/` directory.
2. Activate the plugin through the WordPress admin panel.

**Code**
-----

### nginx-helper-cache-purge.php
```php
<?php
/*
Plugin Name: Nginx Helper Cache Purge
Description: Clears all Nginx helper cache when a plugin or theme is added, updated, or changed.
Version: 1.0
Author: Your Name
Author URI: https://yourwebsite.com
*/

// Define the Nginx helper cache purge function
function nginx_helper_cache_purge() {
    // Get the Nginx helper cache directory
    $cache_dir = WP_CONTENT_DIR . '/nginx-helper/cache/';

    // Check if the cache directory exists
    if (is_dir($cache_dir)) {
        // Get a list of all files in the cache directory
        $files = new RecursiveIteratorIterator(new RecursiveDirectoryIterator($cache_dir));

        // Loop through each file and delete it
        foreach ($files as $file) {
            if ($file->isFile()) {
                unlink($file->getPathname());
            }
        }
    }
}

